WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:19.339
Several trolls were waiting when Morb arrived back at the fortress.

2
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.381
The leader, an especially large and ugly troll, grunted.

3
00:00:23.382 --> 00:00:29.759
A fuzzy image of a figure trapped behind iron bars appeared briefly above his head before quickly fading out.

4
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:37.728
Morb tried to hide his disdain. Trolls were disgusting creatures, with their rough magic and rougher appetites.

5
00:00:37.729 --> 00:00:40.550
But he needed them, at least for now.

6
00:00:40.551 --> 00:00:43.750
"Prepare the treatment!" he ordered the troll.

7
00:00:43.751 --> 00:00:52.524
The troll lumbered off. Morb strode across the room and down a steep stone stairwell.

8
00:00:52.525 --> 00:00:55.080
At the bottom was a heavy wooden door.

9
00:00:55.081 --> 00:00:59.054
As soon as he pushed it open, the prisoners began crying out.

10
00:00:59.055 --> 00:01:05.044
There were now more than a dozen of them in the cells, peering out from behind the heavy iron bars.

11
00:01:05.045 --> 00:01:07.455
But Morb barely looked at most of them.

12
00:01:07.456 --> 00:01:10.785
His eyes went directly to one particular cell.

13
00:01:10.786 --> 00:01:14.785
The long-nosed old man inside stared back defiantly.

14
00:01:14.786 --> 00:01:18.755
His hands and legs were tied so he couldn't move without falling over.

15
00:01:18.756 --> 00:01:22.018
But he stood tall and proud despite the restraints.

16
00:01:22.019 --> 00:01:25.892
"You!" Boz spat out as Morb approached.

17
00:01:25.893 --> 00:01:29.170
"I should have guessed when I heard the news.

18
00:01:29.171 --> 00:01:32.498
You never could accept that you weren't meant to—"

19
00:01:32.499 --> 00:01:39.479
"Silence!" Morb cut him off. He turned toward the door. "I'm ready!" he called loudly.

20
00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:46.779
Heavy footsteps tromped down the stairs. A pair of trolls came in, lugging an iron cauldron between them.

21
00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.623
The prisoners shrank back fearfully when they saw it.

22
00:01:49.624 --> 00:01:54.518
All except Boz. "What are you going to do, Morb?" he demanded.

23
00:01:54.519 --> 00:02:00.625
"Feed me to your pet trolls? The Red Council will hear about this, have no doubt.

24
00:02:00.626 --> 00:02:08.028
Using Flash Freezes and Dousing spells, holding people prisoner . . . You won't get away with it!"

25
00:02:08.029 --> 00:02:12.512
Morb ignored him. The trolls tipped the cauldron, spilling its contents.

26
00:02:12.513 --> 00:02:16.781
Leeches. Dozens of enormous pale blue leeches.

27
00:02:16.782 --> 00:02:19.080
Their faces turned this way and that.

28
00:02:19.081 --> 00:02:23.371
They could sense the powerful magic of all the Red prisoners nearby.

29
00:02:23.372 --> 00:02:30.708
"Get Boz," Morb said. The leeches slowly wriggled between the bars and into Boz's cell.

30
00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:35.828
Boz looked startled. "Where did those things come from?" he exclaimed.

31
00:02:35.829 --> 00:02:41.368
"There are no leeches that size anywhere in Magica! How did you—ahh!"

32
00:02:41.369 --> 00:02:45.403
The rest of his words were lost as the leeches slithered up his legs.

33
00:02:45.404 --> 00:02:50.982
Their pale bodies brightened to a vivid electric blue as they fed on Boz's magic.

34
00:02:50.983 --> 00:02:56.128
Morb watched for a moment, enjoying the sight. Then he turned away.

35
00:02:56.129 --> 00:03:01.627
He still had unfinished business to deal with before he could put the rest of his plan into motion.

36
00:03:01.628 --> 00:03:08.777
He hurried back upstairs, pulled out the picture he'd taken from Boz's house, and carefully ripped out the boy's face.

37
00:03:08.778 --> 00:03:14.551
Morb then stepped toward the Secret Eye, his gaze on the ancient skull at the top.

38
00:03:14.552 --> 00:03:16.803
Then he noticed a flutter of movement.

39
00:03:16.804 --> 00:03:21.615
Turning his head, he saw an insect hovering just outside the window.

40
00:03:21.616 --> 00:03:28.235
"A spy fly!" he murmured. "Now who would want to spy on little old me?"

41
00:03:28.236 --> 00:03:32.492
The spy fly sensed it had been spotted. It spun around to fly off.

42
00:03:32.493 --> 00:03:34.820
But Morb was too quick for it.

43
00:03:34.821 --> 00:03:41.948
Rubbing his fingers together, he blew it to pieces with an extra-strong Flash Freeze.

44
00:03:41.949 --> 00:03:46.997
Then he gently placed the Red boy's picture into one of the skull's eye sockets.

45
00:03:46.998 --> 00:03:53.067
Stepping back, he watched as the map above slowly started to change.

46
00:03:53.068 --> 00:03:57.174
"Stay here," Zann ordered Zing. "We'll be back soon."

47
00:03:57.175 --> 00:04:02.704
The dragon spat fire at him. Zann rolled his eyes.

48
00:04:02.705 --> 00:04:06.450
"Let me talk to him." Darb knelt in front of Zing.

49
00:04:06.451 --> 00:04:10.734
"Listen, buddy. We need you to guard the cave while we check on Gliss, okay?"

50
00:04:10.735 --> 00:04:13.894
Zing continued to look skeptical for a second.

51
00:04:13.895 --> 00:04:18.094
Then finally he whistled happily, wriggling his whole body.

52
00:04:18.095 --> 00:04:24.153
Zann sighed. The dragon never could resist Darb's charms. It was kind of annoying.

53
00:04:24.154 --> 00:04:29.381
"Let's go," Perda said, grabbing Darb's hand. "I've got Darb."

54
00:04:29.382 --> 00:04:34.365
"Meet you in Gliss' living room." Zann closed his eyes, focusing his mind.

55
00:04:34.366 --> 00:04:37.151
This was no time to be sloppy.

56
00:04:37.152 --> 00:04:39.591
He'd been in Gliss' house several times.

57
00:04:39.592 --> 00:04:44.118
Her parents were always inviting him over. It was actually a little embarrassing.

58
00:04:44.119 --> 00:04:51.955
They seemed to think that because Zann and Gliss were the only two Reds in their level, they should be friends. Maybe even more than friends.

59
00:04:51.956 --> 00:04:54.646
Zann tried not to get distracted by that.

60
00:04:54.647 --> 00:04:58.494
He and Gliss weren't especially close, but he liked her fine.

61
00:04:58.495 --> 00:05:03.364
He definitely didn't want to see her captured by this Morb character.

62
00:05:03.365 --> 00:05:07.444
"Zap," he whispered.

63
00:05:07.445 --> 00:05:12.215
Bam! He landed hard on the ground with the wind knocked out of him.

64
00:05:12.216 --> 00:05:15.855
Opening his eyes, he saw Gliss' house.

65
00:05:15.856 --> 00:05:22.607
"Oof!" Perda grunted beside him. She and Darb appeared, both of them also flung off their feet.

66
00:05:22.608 --> 00:05:25.031
"What happened?" Darb asked.

67
00:05:25.032 --> 00:05:29.146
Zann stood up, wincing. "They must have a Shield spell up."

68
00:05:29.147 --> 00:05:33.717
"No wonder," Perda said. "They're probably worried about the warning.

69
00:05:33.718 --> 00:05:36.470
But it means we're blocked out too."

70
00:05:36.471 --> 00:05:46.786
"No big deal," Darb said. "It is possible to get into a house without using magic, you know." He smiled. "It's called knocking on the door."

71
00:05:46.787 --> 00:05:50.565
"Zann!" Gliss' mother exclaimed when she answered the door.

72
00:05:50.566 --> 00:05:54.301
"You shouldn't be out right now. Haven't you heard the news?"

73
00:05:54.302 --> 00:05:56.850
She quickly ushered all the kids inside.

74
00:05:56.851 --> 00:05:59.575
Her husband and Gliss were in the main room.

75
00:05:59.576 --> 00:06:03.767
"You're okay!" Perda exclaimed, rushing over to Gliss.

76
00:06:03.768 --> 00:06:09.322
"Listen," Zann told Gliss' parents. "We just figured out who's behind all the trouble."

77
00:06:09.323 --> 00:06:11.649
"You did?" Gliss' father said.

78
00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:15.744
"I'll show you." Zann snapped his fingers to call up the Directory.

79
00:06:15.745 --> 00:06:18.703
"Morb," he said when the book appeared.

80
00:06:18.704 --> 00:06:23.199
But before the image could fully form, there was a sudden, blinding flash.

81
00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.918
The next thing Zann knew, a familiar figure was standing before him.

82
00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:37.273
"You called?" Morb said with a sneer.
